\section{URL enumeration}{

The portal is server-rendered HTML (no JSON API). Each register's search
listing paginates via a 1-based \code{?pagina=N} query parameter; every page is
one HTML GET that lists the project/plan title, proponent, procedure type,
a detail (\emph{Info}) link and a documentation (\emph{Doc}) link. The page footer
carries a \code{"Pagina X di Y"} counter. The generator advances page-by-page
until it has passed the last page or a page yields no rows. Detail pages
live at \verb{/it-IT/Oggetti/Info/\{id\}}; the detail-page parser is sidecar-first.
}

\section{Geometry}{

None. The portal exposes location only as named Italian text lists
(\emph{Regioni} / \emph{Province} / \emph{Comuni}), surfaced as the \code{regions},
\code{provinces}, and \code{municipalities} extra columns. No coordinate geometry is
available, so \code{geometry_path} / \code{geometry_crs} are never set.
}

\section{Attachments}{

Each record's \emph{Documentazione} index lives at
\verb{/it-IT/Oggetti/Documentazione/\{id\}/\{grp\}} (the \code{{grp}} raggruppamento id
comes from the listing's Doc link or the Info page's procedure table). It is
a paginated \code{?pagina=N} HTML table whose rows carry a \emph{Sezione} (category)
and a direct, public download link
\verb{https://va.mite.gov.it/File/Documento/\{fileId\}} (no authentication; the
server returns \code{application/pdf}). Documents are grouped by their \emph{Sezione};
the handler emits one \verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} / \verb{local_path_<slug>}
list-column per discovered section (the slug is the ASCII-folded \emph{Sezione}
string) plus the deduplicated union in \code{attachment_urls} / \code{local_path}
(required by the schema), following the DE per-section pattern.
}

